    "https://cuny.jobs/684BC992E2814C03B3385A335DAA029825": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Department of Occupational Therapy)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor (Department of Occupational Therapy). Assistant Professor (Department of Occupational Therapy) **FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT** York College, founded in 1966, is a center of academic excellence in the heart of Jamaica, Queens. One of the eleven senior colleges in The City University of New York, the Colleges mission is to enrich students' lives by fostering an environment where theyll grow into passionate and engaged learners. Yorks academic programs are housed in three schools: The School of Arts & Sciences, The School of Business and Information Systems, and The School of Health Sciences and Professional Programs. Over sixty baccalaureate programs from across a variety of disciplines, including accounting, aviation management, business, computer science, journalism, social work, teacher education, a dual BS/MS degree in Occupational Therapy, and one of the top-ranked nursing programs in New York State, provide students with opportunities to study liberal arts, sciences, and professional programs. The College also offers six graduate programs: Aviation Management, Clinical Trials Management, Pharmaceutical Science and Business, Physician Assistant, Social Work and Nursing Education. Located in Queens, the most ethnically diverse county in New York State, the College enrolls 7,000 students from over 95 nations. Nine out of ten students are members of a racial/ethnic minority group, and more than half of undergraduates are the first in their families to pursue higher education. The Colleges 50-acre campus encompasses seven buildings, including science and computer labs, music and television studios, a Performing Arts Center, and a Health and Physical Education Center. The College recently completed seven major construction projects, with more scheduled for the future. In addition, its neighborhood is at the center of a renaissance fueled by economic revitalization. York College is committed to fostering integrity, diversity, intellectual discovery, and civic engagement to benefit its students, the community, and the world. The Department of Occupational Therapy at York College, City University of New York (CUNY) is housed within the School of Health Sciences and Professional Programs. The Department of Occupational Therapy is seeking a qualified candidate for the tenure tract position of Assistant Professor.The anticipated start date is Fall 2027. Responsibilities: 1. Teaching **:** Develop and deliver courses in the occupational therapy curriculum, ensuring high-quality instruction and engaging classroom experiences. 2. Clinical Experience: Bring a minimum of 5 years of clinical experience in physical disabilities, including neuro-rehab, to enhance the practical application of theoretical concepts in the classroom. 3. Scholarly Activities: Engage in scholarly activities, including research, publications, and presentations, contributing to the academic advancement of the department and the field of occupational therapy. 4. Advising: Provide academic and career advising to students, fostering their professional development and success. 5. Service: Participate in departmental and university service activities/assignments, participating in committees and other collaborative initiatives. **QUALIFICATIONS** Ph.D. degree in area(s) of experience or equivalent (OTD). Also required are the ability to teach successfully, demonstrated scholarship or achievement, and ability to cooperate with others for the good of the institution. + Minimum of 5 years of teaching experience in an academic setting. + A minimum of 5 years of clinical experience in occupational therapy. + A minimum of 5 years of clinical experience with physical disabilities, including neurorehab. + Demonstrated ability to engage in scholarly activities. + Must be licensed in the State of New York or eligible for licensing. **Preferred Qualifications:** + Experience with ACOTE Accreditation + Rank of Assistant Professor **COMPENSATION** $98,231 - $105,588 - Salary commensurate with education and experience. CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs. We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. **HOW TO APPLY** Candidates for faculty positions should provide (i) a cover letter explaining interest in, and qualifications for, the position; (ii) curriculum vitae/resume, (iii) evidence of teaching excellence, (iv) a statement of teaching philosophy, (v) a research statement, and (vi) the names, titles, and contact information (telephone and email) for three professional references. Please submit your application online through this job board as follows: Go to www.cuny.edu and click on Employment Select \"Apply Now\" then create or login to a user account and provide the requested information. Click on Job Postings on CUNYfirst Click Search job listings Click on More search options Search by Job Opening ID number 32750 *In order to be considered for this position, applicants must include a cover letter, CV/Resume, and contact information (email and telephone) for three references. Please upload these as ONE document in rtf, doc, or pdf format. **CLOSING DATE** October 30, 2026 (Job posting will be removed at 12am) **JOB SEARCH CATEGORY** CUNY Job Posting: Faculty **EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY** CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply. At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups. Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32750 Location: York College"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/86A27335EAE749F480B2DA7D13586BEF25": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Health Professions)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor (Health Professions). Assistant Professor (Health Professions) **FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT** York College, founded in 1966, is a center of academic excellence in the heart of Jamaica, Queens. One of the eleven senior colleges in The City University of New York, the Colleges mission is to enrich students' lives by fostering an environment where theyll grow into passionate and engaged learners. Yorks academic programs are housed in three schools: The School of Arts & Sciences, The School of Business and Information Systems, and The School of Health Sciences and Professional Programs. Over sixty baccalaureate programs from across a variety of disciplines, including accounting, aviation management, business, computer science, journalism, social work, teacher education, a dual BS/MS degree in Occupational Therapy, and one of the top-ranked nursing programs in New York State, provide students with opportunities to study liberal arts, sciences, and professional programs. The College also offers six graduate programs: Aviation Management, Clinical Trials Management, Pharmaceutical Science and Business, Physician Assistant, Social Work and Nursing Education. Located in Queens, the most ethnically diverse county in New York State, the College enrolls 7,000 students from over 95 nations. Nine out of ten students are members of a racial/ethnic minority group, and more than half of undergraduates are the first in their families to pursue higher education. The Colleges 50-acre campus encompasses seven buildings, including science and computer labs, music and television studios, a Performing Arts Center, and a Health and Physical Education Center. The College recently completed seven major construction projects, with more scheduled for the future. In addition, its neighborhood is at the center of a renaissance fueled by economic revitalization. York College is committed to fostering integrity, diversity, intellectual discovery, and civic engagement to benefit its students, the community, and the world. The Assistant Professor is a full-time, tenure-track position in the Physician Assistant program at York College, CUNY . The program is seeking highly qualified applicants who will serve as principal faculty members, with full participation in teaching in areas of expertise (18-hour credit workload), program administration, development and assessment of curricular content, student advisement, and engaging in productive scholarly research. The successful candidate will be involved in student recruitment and admission activities and provide service to the college and the Health Professions Department, in addition to other related duties. Participation in the programs continuous improvement, ongoing self-study, and accreditation processes is required for this position. Faculty in the PA program are allowed one day per week to practice clinically or engage in professional development activities. The faculty will also function as the Assistant Simulation and Laboratory Coordinator, which includes coordination of the simulation lab; developing and conducting simulation sessions; participation in and coordination of all laboratory-associated administrative tasks including ordering of supplies and equipment, maintenance of equipment, and session scheduling; and coordination of all PA program laboratory sessions (such as Anatomy Laboratory, Physical Diagnosis Laboratory, and Clinical Skills laboratory). A total of three hours of reassigned release time per annum is included for these tasks. Identifies and analyzes clinical curriculum strengths and weaknesses, suggests curriculum enhancements, and implements curricular improvements via the curriculum committee. Responsible for the collection, evaluation, and assessment of didactic and clinical-related data required for accreditation, and participates in the programs ongoing self-study process. **QUALIFICATIONS** + Minimum of a Masters degree required. Doctoral degree preferred. + Graduate of an accredited Physician Assistant Program or a Physician who graduated from an accredited medical school. + Current certification by the National Commission on the Certification of Physician Assistants (NCCPA), if a PA. + Active New York State Physician Assistant License (or eligibility for licensure) or Medical License (MD/DO). + A minimum of three (3) years of clinical experience. + A minimum of one (1) year of teaching experience (may include clinical preceptorship). + Simulation experience preferred **COMPENSATION** $105,588 - $112,841 - Salary commensurate with qualifications and experience. The annual salary is based on a nine-month work year that is paid over the 12-month calendar year. The PA Program operates on an 11-month basis, and faculty who work during the summer months will receive additional compensation at the appropriate CUNY rate. CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs. We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. **HOW TO APPLY** Candidates for faculty positions should provide (i) a cover letter explaining interest in, and qualifications for, the position; (ii) curriculum vitae/resume, (iii) evidence of teaching excellence, (iv) a statement of teaching philosophy, (v) a research statement, and (vi) the names, titles, and contact information (telephone and email) for three professional references. Please submit your application online through this job board as follows: Go to www.cuny.edu and click on Employment Select \"Apply Now\" then create or login to a user account and provide the requested information. Click on Job Postings on CUNYfirst Click Search job listings Click on More search options Search by Job Opening ID number 32006 *In order to be considered for this position, applicants must include a cover letter, CV/Resume, and contact information (email and telephone) for three references. Please upload these as ONE document in rtf, doc, or pdf format. **CLOSING DATE** *Revised November 23, 2026 (Posting will be removed at 12am) **JOB SEARCH CATEGORY** CUNY Job Posting: Faculty **EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY** CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply. At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups. Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32006 Location: York College"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/8AB6C55B464E476BA947EA78D1528C8B25": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - (Behavioral Sciences)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor - (Behavioral Sciences). Assistant Professor - (Behavioral Sciences) **FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT** York College, founded in 1966, is a center of academic excellence in the heart of Jamaica, Queens. One of the eleven senior colleges in The City University of New York, the Colleges mission is to enrich students' lives by fostering an environment where theyll grow into passionate and engaged learners. Yorks academic programs are housed in three schools: The School of Arts & Sciences, The School of Business and Information Systems, and The School of Health Sciences and Professional Programs. Over sixty baccalaureate programs from across a variety of disciplines, including accounting, aviation management, business, computer science, journalism, social work, teacher education, a dual BS/MS degree in Occupational Therapy, and one of the top-ranked nursing programs in New York State, provide students with opportunities to study liberal arts, sciences, and professional programs. The College also offers six graduate programs: Aviation Management, Clinical Trials Management, Pharmaceutical Science and Business, Physician Assistant, Social Work and Nursing Education. Located in Queens, the most ethnically diverse county in New York State, the College enrolls over 7,000 students from over 95 nations. Nine out of ten students are members of a racial/ethnic minority group, and more than half of undergraduates are the first in their families to pursue higher education. The Colleges 50-acre campus encompasses seven buildings, including science and computer labs, music and television studios, a Performing Arts Center, and a Health and Physical Education Center. The College recently completed seven major construction projects, with more scheduled for the future. In addition, its neighborhood is at the center of a renaissance fueled by economic revitalization. York College is committed to fostering integrity, diversity, intellectual discovery, and civic engagement to benefit its students, the community, and the world. The Behavioral Sciences Department at York College, one of 11 senior colleges of the City University of New York, one of the most culturally diverse institutions of higher education in the United States. We invite applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty position in psychology at the rank of Assistant Professor to begin Fall 2027. The Department of Behavioral Sciences is a multidisciplinary department including the Psychology, Sociology, and Political Science disciplines. We seek candidates who have an active program of research that provides opportunities for the participation of undergraduate students. Applicants should be able to teach a range of courses in Psychology including Statistics, Physiology of Behavior, Cognitive Psychology, and Experimental Psychology. Applicants should be comfortable teaching in various modalities (i.e., online, in-person). Reporting to the Chair of the Department of Behavioral Sciences, the Assistant Professors responsibilities will include, but not be limited to: + Teaching psychology courses in the in-person, hybrid, and online formats. + Participating in the development and assessment of new curricula and pedagogical approaches. + Providing student advisement and mentoring. + Contributing to Department, School, College, and University service activities, including governance, program assessment, day-to-day operation, and student recruitment and retention, among other areas. + Research resulting in publications and presentations. + Collaboration with colleagues to support departmental initiatives and college-wide programs. **QUALIFICATIONS** Ph.D. in Psychology. Also required are the ability to teach successfully, demonstrated scholarship or achievement, and ability to collaborate with others for the good of the program and institution. **PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS** + Prior teaching experience at the college level. + Active research agenda that includes recent publications and presentations. + Strong interpersonal and communication skills and a commitment to collaborative work. + Can teach courses in Statistics, Physiology of Behavior, Cognitive Psychology, and/or Experimental Psychology in a variety of modalities. + Can teach students of diverse backgrounds including those from a pluralistic, urban environment in which a substantial proportion of students are first-generation college students. **COMPENSATION** $76,041 - $98,231. Salary commensurate with education and experience. CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs. We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. **HOW TO APPLY** Candidates for faculty positions should provide (i) a cover letter explaining interest in, and qualifications for, the position; (ii) curriculum vitae/resume, (iii) evidence of teaching excellence, (iv) a statement of teaching philosophy, (v) a research statement, and (vi) the names, titles, and contact information (telephone and email) for three professional references. Please submit your application online through this job board as follows: Go to www.cuny.edu and click on Employment Select \"Apply Now\" then create or login to a user account and provide the requested information. Click on Job Postings on CUNYfirst Click Search job listings Click on More search options Search by Job Opening ID number 32876 *In order to be considered for this position, applicants must include a cover letter, CV/Resume, and contact information (email and telephone) for three references. Please upload these as ONE document in rtf, doc, or pdf format. **CLOSING DATE** December 30, 2026 (Job posting will be removed at 12am) **JOB SEARCH CATEGORY** CUNY Job Posting: Faculty **EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY** CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply. At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups. Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32876 Location: York College"
